msgid "RAM mapper:"
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:660
msgid "Auto (off when a tape starts the machine)"
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:661
msgid "On (128K of mapper RAM)"
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:662
msgid "Off (64K of RAM, as an MSX1)"
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:663
msgid "The memory mapper answers at ports FCh-FFh. Some tape games (the ZX Spectrum conversions) write to port FEh for their own purposes and, with the mapper there, move the RAM under themselves; Auto leaves the mapper off when Auto load starts a tape. Takes effect with the next reset"
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:667
msgid "MSX-DOS 2 needs the mapper."
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:668
msgid "MSX 1 compatibility mode"
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:669
msgid "Some MSX1 programs use FFFFh as ordinary RAM or look for RAM in a primary slot alone, which the MSX2's expanded slot 3 breaks. With this on no slot is expanded (the RAM is slot 3 alone, the sub-ROM is in slot 2) and there is no disk drive. It is also in the Options menu. Resets the machine"
msgstr ""

#: SettingsForm.pas:676
